/OPBaseFont2 13 Tf
(TO THE HONORABLE SPECIAL COURT OF REVIEW:) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 678.2 Tm
105 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(The Honorable Sharon Keller, Presiding Judge of the Texas Court of Criminal) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 648.25 Tm
104 Tz
(Appeals \(the “CCA”\), files this Reply in support of her Motion to Dismiss, and would) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 618.25 Tm
99 Tz
(show the Special Court of Review the following.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 588.2 Tm
109 Tz
/OPBaseFont2 13 Tf
(I. THE ORDER IS UNCONSTITUTIONAL) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 561.399 Tm
100 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(When construing the Texas Constitution, courts “rely heavily on its literal text and) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 531.599 Tm
103 Tz
(must give effect to its plain language.” ) Tj
1 0 0 1 284.4 531.599 Tm
102 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 13 Tf
(Stringer v. Cendant Mortgage Corp., ) Tj
1 0 0 1 484.3 531.599 Tm
100 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(23 S.W.3d) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 501.599 Tm
104 Tz
(353, 355 \(Tex. 2000\). Where, as in this case, the Constitution’s language is “clear and) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 471.599 Tm
106 Tz
(unambiguous, [the Court] must apply its words according to their common meaning) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 441.849 Tm
103 Tz
(without resort to rules of construction or extrinsic aids.” ) Tj
1 0 0 1 379.45 441.849 Tm
101 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 13 Tf
(State v. Shumake, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 478.55 441.799 Tm
99 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(199 S.W.3d) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 411.849 Tm
103 Tz
(279, 284 \(Tex. 2006\) \(construing statute\). Here, the SCJC resorts to deleting text from) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 382.099 Tm
99 Tz
(the Constitution in order to reach its desired conclusion.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 352.299 Tm
105 Tz
(As explained in Judge Keller’s Motion, the SCJC’s Order, and Rule 10\(m\), on) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 322.349 Tm
104 Tz
(which it is based, conflict with the Texas Constitution. The Constitution plainly states) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 292.349 Tm
102 Tz
(that, once the SCJC initiates formal proceedings against a judge, the only punishment it) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 262.299 Tm
110 Tz
(may impose is a censure or a recommendation to remove the judge. To repeat the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 232.6 Tm
99 Tz
(pertinent language of the Constitution for this Court yet again:) Tj
1 0 0 1 144 202.6 Tm
100 Tz
(After such investigation as it deems necessary, the Commission may) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 187.699 Tm
103 Tz
(in its discretion issue a private or public admonition, warning, reprimand,) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.25 172.799 Tm
101 Tz
(or requirement that the person obtain additional training or education, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 480.25 173.049 Tm
110 Tz
/OPBaseFont1 12 Tf
(or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 496.1 173 Tm
107 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(if) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 157.699 Tm
105 Tz
(the Commission determines that the situation merits such action, it may) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 142.799 Tm
101 Tz
(institute formal proceedings and order a formal hearing to be held before it) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.25 127.949 Tm
99 Tz
(concerning the censure, removal, or retirement of a person holding an office) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.7 113.049 Tm
108 Tz
(. . . or it may in its discretion request the Supreme Court to appoint an) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 97.899 Tm
101 Tz
(active or retired District Judge . . . as a Master to hear and take evidence in) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 83.049 Tm
108 Tz
(any such matter, and to report thereon to the Commission. . . . If, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 479.3 83.049 Tm
102 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 13 Tf
(after) Tj
1 0 0 1 295.699 49.449 Tm
109 Tz
(- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 304.1 49.449 Tm
87 Tz
