(Q. Let me focus on the phrase court rule. Why is the oral tradition later) Tj
1 0 0 1 144 692.899 Tm
114 Tz
(reduced to writing? That the oral tradition of the court protocol on) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.5 678 Tm
106 Tz
(September 25th is not a court rule within the meaning of the canon that) Tj
1 0 0 1 144 663.1 Tm
99 Tz
(you're accused of violating?) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 636.25 Tm
109 Tz
(A. A court rule is something that is promulgated by a Supreme Court or the) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.25 621.149 Tm
101 Tz
(Court of Criminal Appeals, usually by the Supreme Court that is published) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.25 606.25 Tm
98 Tz
(for comment and reviewed and then adopted.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 579.399 Tm
101 Tz
(S. Keller Test., Tr. vol. 4, at 43:5-16 \(App. Vol. 2 U\). Indeed, when the Special Counsel) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 549.35 Tm
99 Tz
(asked Judge Keller whether the oral protocol was a duty of office, she said no:) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.25 519.599 Tm
109 Tz
(Q. Don’t you agree that part of your duties of office as a judge of the Texas) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.25 504.5 Tm
99 Tz
(Court of Criminal Appeals included, as with other judges, the responsibility) Tj
1 0 0 1 144 489.599 Tm
(to abide by the execution day procedures?) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 462.949 Tm
93 Tz
(A.) Tj
1 0 0 1 119.75 462.949 Tm
2000 Tz
(\t) Tj
1 0 0 1 144 462.699 Tm
104 Tz
(No, I would say that my responsibility to the other judges required me to) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.5 447.599 Tm
98 Tz
(abide by the procedures.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 420.949 Tm
105 Tz
(S. Keller Test., Tr. vol. 4, at 7:16-21 \(App. Vol. 2 U\). The SCJC’s footnote argument) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 390.949 Tm
102 Tz
(that somehow Judge Keller testified that the oral protocol constituted a duty of office is) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 360.949 Tm
98 Tz
(conclusively refuted by the record.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 330.949 Tm
101 Tz
(Second, and more significantly, judges do not make up the duties of their offices;) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 301.199 Tm
100 Tz
(the office exists independently of the individual occupying it, and the duties of the office) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 271.199 Tm
101 Tz
(are established by law, not by the individual. The rules and laws governing Judge Keller) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 241.449 Tm
(and the CCA are codified in article 5 of the Texas Constitution, chapter 22 of the Texas) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 211.449 Tm
105 Tz
(Government Code, and the Texas Rules of Appellate Procedure. Judge Keller did not) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 181.649 Tm
98 Tz
(violate any of those rules and laws.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 151.649 Tm
101 Tz
(The SCJC cannot prosecute and discipline a judge unless they violate a law, court) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 121.899 Tm
100 Tz
(rule, or duty of office. The “oral protocol” simply was not a duty of office.) Tj
