/OPBaseFont2 12 Tf
(IV. JUDGE BERCHELMANN EXONERATED JUDGE KELLER) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 680.85 Tm
102 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(The Commission argues that Judge Berchelmann did not exonerate Judge Keller) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 651.1 Tm
101 Tz
(of the charges brought against her because he made some comments which were critical) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 621.149 Tm
107 Tz
(of her. There is no question that Judge Berchelmann did not find Judge Keller to be) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 591.35 Tm
112 Tz
(flawless; but that is not what the August 2009 trial was about, nor is it what this) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 561.35 Tm
104 Tz
(proceeding concerns. The trial concerned one issue: did Judge Keller violate any law,) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 531.599 Tm
107 Tz
(rule, code, or canon of judicial conduct. Judge Berchelmann said, quite clearly, that) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 501.599 Tm
99 Tz
(Judge Keller had not violated any written or unwritten rule or law.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 471.599 Tm
100 Tz
(That said, it is undeniable that Judge Berchelmann found fault with Judge Keller’s) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 441.849 Tm
107 Tz
(conduct on September 25, 2007. The most that can be said of Judge Berchelmann’s) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 411.849 Tm
112 Tz
(criticism, however, is that he found that Judge Keller erred in her judgment that) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 382.099 Tm
104 Tz
(afternoon. But an error in judgment is not cause for any sort of judicial discipline; the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 352.099 Tm
107 Tz
(case law plainly holds that discipline may only be imposed for willful misconduct –) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 322.549 Tm
104 Tz
(conduct which constitutes “intentional or grossly indifferent misuse of judicial office,) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 292.549 Tm
103 Tz
(involving more than an error of judgment or lack of diligence.” ) Tj
1 0 0 1 418.55 292.299 Tm
126 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 11 Tf
(In re Bell, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 478.1 292.349 Tm
100 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(894 S.W.2d) Tj
1 0 0 1 73.45 262.35 Tm
105 Tz
(119, 126 \(Tex. Spec. Ct. Rev. 1995\) \(citing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 314.9 262.299 Tm
128 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 11 Tf
(In re Thoma, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 391.9 262.299 Tm
103 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(873 S.W.2d 477, 489 \(Tex.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 232.799 Tm
101 Tz
(Rev. Trib. 1994\)\). “Willful conduct requires a showing of bad faith, including a specific) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 202.549 Tm
102 Tz
(intent to use the powers of office to accomplish an end which the judge knew or should) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 172.799 Tm
104 Tz
(have known was beyond the legitimate exercise of authority.” ) Tj
1 0 0 1 412.55 172.799 Tm
158 Tz
/OPBaseFont3 11 Tf
(Id. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 435.85 172.799 Tm
100 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(Judge Berchelmann) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 142.799 Tm
101 Tz
(found that Judge Keller did not commit any willful misconduct. Nor has there ever been) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 113.049 Tm
103 Tz
(any showing that she misused her office, as the case law requires, notwithstanding the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 83.049 Tm
99 Tz
(SCJC’s pronouncements in its unconstitutional Order.) Tj
